1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch====
2 CONT  English FROM M A N N 31 M A R C H 1744 NS Austrians if they should attempt to follow the Spaniards. The day of his departure, the 25th inst., a manifest20 was published to acquaint the world with his reasons for so doing.21 His l
2 CONC ittle Queen and little daughter departed the same day for Gaeta.22 W e shall soon see what this produces. Things there are in great confusion; a viceroy23 is appointed during his absence. I had a great mind to send you the manifes
2 CONC t, but it is extreme long, and I believe you would not give a farthing to see it. Perhaps it may be published in the Gazette, for I send it, with its translation, to his Grace.24 It is so verbose, and such nonsense in Italian, tha
2 CONC t I had much to do to make it intelligible in English. W e have a thousand reports about the French fleet and transports: some say they have been dispersed by a storm,25 and that Sir John Norris has defeated a part of them. M r Ma
2 CONC thews was the 1 ith inst. at Mahone with all his fleet,26 but designed to return to Hieres. We fancy he will alter his resolution when he hears that the French and Spanish squadrons are in separate ports, the first in Alicant,27 w
2 CONC here the seamen say he can easily demolish them if they stay for his arrival, but we fear they may get into a better port. W h a t fools they were, not to prepare for an embarkation which might have passed into Italy during the ab
2 CONC sence of our fleet. Adieu, m y dear child. Pray send m e word that Sir John Norris has cover their sentiments ... on the slightest suspicion whole families are put into prison . . . from all which people are inclined to believe th
2 CONC at a general insurrection would ensue' (ibid. f. 83). 20. 'Declaration published on the departure of the King of the Two Sicilies from the city of Naples towards the frontiers,' dated 'Naples, March 25th, 1744' (see n. 24 below). 
2 CONC 21. It enumerates grievances against Great Britain, and justifies the measures taken in view of the 'treacherous designs against the T w o Sicilies' concealed 'with so little caution' by the 'ministers of the Court of Vienna.' 22.
2 CONC  40 miles north-west of Naples.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 23. '''A regency composed of three secretaries of state as councillors and Don Michael Reggio, general of the galleys, as president or viceroy. (Newsletter of 31 March NS under date of  Naples March 24th, S.P. 98/48 f. 104). Don
2 CONC  Michele Reggio e Branciforte, Knight of Malta and captain-general of the galleys, was made member of the royal council of Naples in 1762''' 
2 CONT * Vittorio Spreti, Enciclopedia storiconobiliare italiana, Milan 1928-36, v. 643;
