1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The father of Orlando Amato senior is not documented in any of the available evidence. His wife was NOT Margherita Amato (she was the wife of his grandson Orlando). A Caterina, widow of Orlando, is documented in th
2 CONC e notary registers of the State Archives of Sciacca as early as 9 Sept 1435 (ASX, Not. Andrea Liotta reg. 2 c.100r). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was still alive as late as 16 March 1434 when he, along with others, presented petitions to impose a differentiated monthly tax to raise money needed for the repair of the city walls of Sciacca (Real Cancelleria 69, fol. 102v-1
2 CONC 06v).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the inventory of the assets of the late Orlando Amato, recorded on 28 September 1435, it states that the deceased had been married to Caterina, that the eldest son and heir of the feudal assets was Giuseppe Amato, and that the 
2 CONC other assets were devolved to the sons Giovanni, Matteo and Amato (ASX, Andrea Liota, reg. 2, cc. 113v-115r). 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Feudum Zaffuto vulgo nuncupatum in Valle Mazarie positum per quondam Orlandum de Amato Seniorem ut asseritur et de inde per Ioseph de Amato ejus filium antiquitus possidebatur tamen de illis Regia in Cancellaria nullus apparet tit
2 CONC ulus sive privilegium. Tandem Ioseph predictus pro se suisque heredibus ejus de corpore legitime descendentibus jure francorum de feudo ipso a tunc Regni pro Regibus juxta formam Capitulorum Serenissimi Regis Al fonsi antiquis Reg
2 CONC ijs regalijs reservari solitis et consuetis semper salvis, VI Ianuarii II Indicionis 1453 investituram reportavit.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''English translation''':
2 CONT
2 CONT The fief commonly called Zaffuto in the Mazarie Valley was placed by the former Orlando de Amato Senior, as is alleged, and from there was anciently possessed by Joseph de Amato his son, however, no title or privilege appears abou
2 CONC t them in the Royal Chancellery. Finally, the aforementioned Joseph, for himself and his heirs of his body legitimately descending by the law of the Franks, from the fief itself from that time on for the Kings according to the for
2 CONC m of the Chapters of the Most Serene King Alfonso, always preserved and accustomed to be reserved for ancient Kings and Queens, received the investiture on 6 January 1453 by the Second Indiction.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.google.com/books/edition/I_Capibrevi_ora_per_la_prima_volta_pubbl/Dk0bAQAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1
