1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On the 9th and 12th of September 1435, Caterina, widow of Orlando Amato, represented by Giovanni Lucchesi, sold 4 kantars of sheep cheese each to Muxa Schichina and Fariono Schichina, Jews of Sciacca, at a price of
2 CONC  9 tari a kantar (ASX, Andrea Liota, reg. 2, cc. 100r, 109v, respectively). On 17 September 1435, she sold 1,020 sheep to Nicolo and Perino Bruxa, father and son from Sciacca, at the price of 4.9 ounces per hundred (cc. 106r-v). O
2 CONC n 28 October 1435, she sold 1 kantar of sheep cheese to Xilomello and Saccarello de Sagulori, Jews of Sciacca, at a price of 8.1 tari (c. 125r). Caterina's family of origin is evident from a document in which she named her brother
2 CONC  Ferrando Lucchesi as her representative in a declaration on 12 October 1435 (cc. 118v-119r).
